msgid "Open Terminal"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:227
msgid "What the prompt means"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:227
msgid ""
"The prompt is the text before the cursor. It shows that the terminal is "
"ready for a command. Type after it; do not type the prompt itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:228
msgid "Run a command"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:228
msgid ""
"Type a command and press Enter to run it. For example, pwd shows the current "
"folder and ls lists its files. These commands only show information."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:229
msgid "Read the result"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:229
msgid ""
"Commands may print information or an error message. Read the last lines "
"first. If a command finishes without an error, it may return to the prompt "
"without printing anything."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:230
msgid "Move between folders"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:230
msgid ""
"Use cd Documents to enter a folder and cd .. to go up one level. Use pwd to "
"check where you are."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:231
msgid "Use Tab and command history"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:231
msgid ""
"Press Tab to complete a file or folder name when it is unique. Press the Up "
"Arrow to find a command you used earlier; check it before pressing Enter."
msgstr ""

